## 1. OAuth2LoginConfigurer → `ServerHttpSecurity.oauth2Login()`

The reactive `OAuth2LoginSpec` exposes equivalent methods. Note the key naming differences:

| WebMVC (`OAuth2LoginConfigurer`) | WebFlux (`OAuth2LoginSpec`) |
|---|---|
| `redirectionEndpoint()` | `authenticationMatcher(ServerWebExchangeMatcher)` |
| `failureHandler(...)` | `authenticationFailureHandler(ServerAuthenticationFailureHandler)` |
| `successHandler(...)` | `authenticationSuccessHandler(ServerAuthenticationSuccessHandler)` |
| `defaultSuccessUrl(url)` | `authenticationSuccessHandler(new RedirectServerAuthenticationSuccessHandler(url))` |
| `tokenEndpoint().accessTokenResponseClient(...)` | `authenticationManager(...)` with a `WebClientReactive...TokenResponseClient` |

The full set of reactive options: oauth2Login can be configured with authenticationConverter, authenticationMatcher, authenticationManager, authenticationSuccessHandler, authenticationFailureHandler, clientRegistrationRepository, authorizedClientRepository, authorizedClientService, authorizationRequestResolver, authorizationRequestRepository, and securityContextRepository.

```java
http.oauth2Login(oauth2 -> oauth2
    // redirectEndpoint() equivalent — set the callback/redirect matcher
    .authenticationMatcher(new PathPatternParserServerWebExchangeMatcher(
        "/login/oauth2/code/{registrationId}"))
    // failureHandler() equivalent
    .authenticationFailureHandler(new RedirectServerAuthenticationFailureHandler("/login?error"))
    // successHandler() / defaultSuccessUrl() equivalent
    .authenticationSuccessHandler(new RedirectServerAuthenticationSuccessHandler("/home"))
    // tokenEndpoint() equivalent — customize via the authenticationManager
    .authenticationManager(authManager)
);
```

Important detail about the redirection endpoint: the OAuth2LoginSecurityConfig sets the authenticationMatcher with a PathPatternParserServerWebExchangeMatcher for "/login/oauth2/callback/{registrationId}". So your MVC `redirectionEndpoint().baseUri(...)` maps to `authenticationMatcher(...)`.

For the `tokenEndpoint()` (custom token response client), you wire it through the `authenticationManager` using the reactive token response client: create a WebClientReactiveAuthorizationCodeTokenResponseClient, add a parameters converter to it, and pass it into a DelegatingReactiveAuthenticationManager combining OidcAuthorizationCodeReactiveAuthenticationManager and OAuth2LoginReactiveAuthenticationManager via oauth2Login.authenticationManager(...).

```java
WebClientReactiveAuthorizationCodeTokenResponseClient tokenResponseClient =
    new WebClientReactiveAuthorizationCodeTokenResponseClient();
// tokenResponseClient.addParametersConverter(...);  // custom token endpoint params

ReactiveAuthenticationManager authManager = new DelegatingReactiveAuthenticationManager(
    new OidcAuthorizationCodeReactiveAuthenticationManager(
        tokenResponseClient, new OidcReactiveOAuth2UserService()),
    new OAuth2LoginReactiveAuthenticationManager(
        tokenResponseClient, new DefaultReactiveOAuth2UserService())
);
```

